<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand Marcos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand Marcos was President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1965 to 1986. He declared martial law in 1972 and ruled as a dictator, jailing opponents and enriching his family and cronies on a vast scale. The assassination of the opposition leader Benigno Aquino in 1983 and a fraudulent election in 1986 provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/people-power-revolution">People Power Revolution</a>, which drove him into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos.jpg" alt="Ferdinand Marcos" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Malacañang Press · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_Marcos%27_official_portrait_during_his_second_term_(1969)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
